description:
If we look at Plannotator README (https://github.com/backnotprop/plannotator/blob/main/apps/hook/README.md) there is a sentence:

> Manual Installation (Hooks)
>
>If you prefer not to use the plugin system

That would seem to imply that if the plugin is installed the manual installation of hooks is not needed. But when I use Claude recently on WSL2, I found that no Plannotator UI got invoked on ExitPlan. So it seems like the hook install is indeed needed:


> add this to your ~/.claude/settings.json:
>
> ```json
> {
>   "hooks": {
>     "PermissionRequest": [
>       {
>         "matcher": "ExitPlanMode",
>         "hooks": [
>           {
>             "type": "command",
>             "command": "plannotator",
>             "timeout": 345600
>           }
>         ]
>       }
>     ]
>   }
> }
> ```
